# An 8-bit text has no surrogates, so `codePointAt` in its loop is `charCodeAt`: a load of a byte, written out eight times, and no unit is compared with 0xD800.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 8
# CHECK-COUNT-8: Int32 b@{{*}} = Load8Z(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:characters8,
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:characters
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 8
# HOT-NOT: Branch(
# HOT-NOT: $55296(
# HOT-NOT: isLoopPoll
# HOT-NOT: Reads:StringImpl
# HOT-NOT: Reads:JSRopeString
# HOT-NOT: ExitsSideways
# HOT: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:Less)
# HOT-NOT: Branch(
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# The loop for 16-bit characters stays in line as long as no unit is a surrogate.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 1
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 1
# HOT: Int32 b@[[unit]] = Load16Z(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:characters16,
# HOT: Int32 b@[[isPlain]] = Below(b@[[unit]], $55296(
# HOT-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isPlain]], Terminal,
# HOT-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
